From 83d06eac85266d4f8a5a4c7a7c97729d0b0e13bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 09:11:47 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: apple: mca: Bound the PCM buffer size again

Commit 79af0bae4d0d ("ASoC: apple: mca: Make the capture buffers
cacheable") stopped preallocating the capture buffers, so they are now
allocated at hw_params to the buffer's own size. The 3 MiB preallocation
was also what bounded the capture buffer: the core sets a substream's
buffer_bytes_max to its preallocated size, and the runtime hardware
leaves it at SIZE_MAX. Without a preallocation the sense PCM offers
buffers of up to 4 GiB.

speakersafetyd sets no buffer size on the speaker sense PCM, so alsa-lib
picks the largest buffer and the NONCOHERENT allocation fails:

  snd_pcm_hw_params failed with error 'Out of memory (12)'

speakersafetyd then panics and restarts in a loop. It never takes the
speaker volume lock, and the speakers stay at the kernel's floor, with
no sound on every MCA Mac it protects (seen on a J316 on
7.3.0-26.fc45.aurora, the kernel with the legacy unlock interface).

Bound the PCM buffer at 3 MiB, the playback preallocation's size and
the limit capture had before 79af0bae4d0d. Clients that size their own
buffer (speakerguardd, PipeWire) ask for far less and are unaffected.

Fixes: 79af0bae4d0d ("ASoC: apple: mca: Make the capture buffers cacheable")
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
---
 sound/soc/apple/mca.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/apple/mca.c b/sound/soc/apple/mca.c
index 69abfcda7e813..18d73b50af861 100644
--- a/sound/soc/apple/mca.c
+++ b/sound/soc/apple/mca.c
@@ -127,6 +127,9 @@
 			   SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE | \
 			   SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S32_LE)
 
+/* Largest PCM buffer, and the playback preallocation: 3 MiB. */
+#define MCA_BUFFER_BYTES_MAX (512 * 1024 * 6)
+
 struct mca_cluster {
 	int no;
 	__iomem void *base;
@@ -962,7 +965,15 @@ static int mca_set_runtime_hwparams(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 	hw.periods_max = UINT_MAX;
 	hw.period_bytes_min = 256;
 	hw.period_bytes_max = dma_get_max_seg_size(dma_dev);
-	hw.buffer_bytes_max = SIZE_MAX;
+	/*
+	 * The capture buffer is not preallocated (see mca_pcm_new()), so the
+	 * core does not bound it by a preallocation: bound it here, at the size
+	 * the playback preallocation (and formerly the capture one) allows. An
+	 * unbounded maximum lets a client that sets no buffer size, such as
+	 * speakersafetyd on the speaker sense PCM, ask for gigabytes and fail
+	 * hw_params with -ENOMEM.
+	 */
+	hw.buffer_bytes_max = MCA_BUFFER_BYTES_MAX;
 	hw.fifo_size = 16;
 
 	ret = snd_dmaengine_pcm_refine_runtime_hwparams(substream, &dma_data,
@@ -1245,7 +1256,7 @@ static int mca_pcm_new(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 						   chan->device->dev, 0, SIZE_MAX);
 		else
 			snd_pcm_set_managed_buffer(substream, SNDRV_DMA_TYPE_DEV_IRAM,
-						   chan->device->dev, 512 * 1024 * 6,
+						   chan->device->dev, MCA_BUFFER_BYTES_MAX,
 						   SIZE_MAX);
 	}
 
-- 
